\paragraph{Future directions.}
Per-step process rewards offer the most direct path forward: SMART~\citep{beigi2025smart} succeeds at sycophancy calibration by evaluating behavioral transitions at individual reasoning steps, capturing temporal structure that scalar per-completion rewards compress away.
More broadly, condition-aware rewards that incorporate evidential warrant deserve investigation; whether attributes with similar geometric entanglement~\citep{skalse2022hacking} exhibit the same failures remains open.

\paragraph{Sycophancy Characterization and Mitigation.}
Sycophancy is pervasive in RLHF-trained assistants \citep{sharma2023sycophancy, shapira2026amplifies} and traceable to late-layer preference shifts \citep{wang2025internal}; mitigations span synthetic data \citep{wei2024synthetic}, consistency training \citep{consistency2025bctact}, and neuron-level correction \citep{obrien2025fewbadneurons}.
\citet{vennemeyer2025sycophancy} show that sycophancy decomposes into independently steerable sub-behaviors; a single $\dsyc$ captures only their shared variance, which is why the step from diagnosis to reward is structurally blocked.

